{"authored" [{"question" "q-318988" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $p=⟨9,12,0⟩$ and $q=⟨0,3,4⟩.$ Find ${\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p-{\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q.$\n\n${\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p-{\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fffea451a819647cab98429e526789880fb1f7c85cb6c6904836215f7a554e2" "basis" 656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-318988" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Using the scalar projection formula, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p & =\\frac{p\\cdot q}{|\\,q\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{p}_{x}{q}_{x}+{p}_{y}{q}_{y}+{p}_{z}{q}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{q}_{x}^{2}+{q}_{y}^{2}+{q}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(9)(0)+(12)(3)+(0)(4)}{\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{3}^{2}+{4}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{\\sqrt{25}} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q & =\\frac{p\\cdot q}{|\\,p\\,|} \\\\  & =\\frac{{p}_{x}{q}_{x}+{p}_{y}{q}_{y}+{p}_{z}{q}_{z}}{\\sqrt{{p}_{x}^{2}+{p}_{y}^{2}+{p}_{z}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{\\sqrt{{9}^{2}+{12}^{2}+{0}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{36}{\\sqrt{225}} \\\\  & =\\frac{12}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{comp}}_{q}\\,p-{\\text{comp}}_{p}\\,q & =\\frac{36}{5}-\\frac{12}{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{24}{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fffea451a819647cab98429e526789880fb1f7c85cb6c6904836215f7a554e2" "basis" 656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-318988" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "063df9d32c7b7bbea1e614df42642d34cda64b6b0566b4034b16eb743f7d8016" "basis" 656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-318988" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fffea451a819647cab98429e526789880fb1f7c85cb6c6904836215f7a554e2" "basis" 656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-318988" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{24}{5}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fffea451a819647cab98429e526789880fb1f7c85cb6c6904836215f7a554e2" "basis" 656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-237018" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Let $a=5i-4j+3k$ and $b=-7i+xj+k.$ Given that the scalar projection of $a$ onto $b$ is zero, find the value of $x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fffea451a819647cab98429e526789880fb1f7c85cb6c6904836215f7a554e2" "basis" 656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-237018" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its scalar projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals zero only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =5\\cdot (-7)+(-4)\\cdot x+3\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-4x-32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ -4x-32 & =0 \\\\ 4x & =-32 \\\\ x & =-8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fffea451a819647cab98429e526789880fb1f7c85cb6c6904836215f7a554e2" "basis" 656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-237018" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "063df9d32c7b7bbea1e614df42642d34cda64b6b0566b4034b16eb743f7d8016" "basis" 656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-237018" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/state.json" "file_sha256" "3fffea451a819647cab98429e526789880fb1f7c85cb6c6904836215f7a554e2" "basis" 656 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-237018" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "-4"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13965088/state.json" 